WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.440
A prophetic dream that changes&nbsp;
everything we knew about "Game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.280
of Thrones!" And it happens in the very&nbsp;
first episode of "House of the Dragon."

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.720
It's no secret that Game of Thrones Season 8&nbsp;
received an astounding amount of backlash from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.760
fans and critics alike, but the most&nbsp;
baffling element of the entire season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.960
might be the fact that the series finale left so&nbsp;
many questions unanswered. One of the most obvious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.240
examples of this is the mysterious backstory&nbsp;
of the White Walkers, a group of demonic ice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.760
creatures who invade Westeros from the far north&nbsp;
with an army of the undead. These beings may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.080
extinguished life across the entire continent,&nbsp;
were it not for the Battle of Winterfell.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.160
The threat of the White Walkers ends with the&nbsp;
death of the Night King at the hands of Arya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.200
Stark. Afterwards, the series protagonists set&nbsp;
their sights on King's Landing and the threat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.400
of Cersei Lannister, and the White Walkers&nbsp;
are barely even mentioned. As such, we never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.160
receive any concrete answers about who the White&nbsp;
Walkers really are, or what their purpose is.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.840
One of the most mysterious aspects&nbsp;
of the White Walkers is their strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.880
connection to the dragon-riding Targaryen&nbsp;
family. Both factions are integral to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.160
ancient prophecy involving Azor Ahai, often&nbsp;
known as "the prince that was promised."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.840
Now, it seems possible that we might actually gain&nbsp;
some concrete information about this relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.680
as HBO's House of the Dragon has already answered&nbsp;
a huge question Game of Thrones left in its wake.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.320
One major mystery at the heart of Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.600
as well as the books on which it was based, is the&nbsp;
motive behind Aegon the Conqueror's invasion of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.840
Westeros. George R.R. Martin's Fire &amp; Blood claims&nbsp;
that Aegon only invaded the continent after being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:43.440
insulted by the Storm King Argilac Durrandon ,&nbsp;
and that his abrupt call to arms was precipitated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.880
by his own belief that the Seven Kingdoms of&nbsp;
Westeros ought to be united into one nation.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.720
However, Episode 1 of House of the&nbsp;
Dragon, "The Heirs of the Dragon,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.920
reveals that this isn't actually true, and&nbsp;
finally gives fans a definitive answer for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:03.040
why Aegon decided to conquer Westeros in&nbsp;
the first place. King Viserys tells his heir&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.640
Rhaenyra Targaryen that Aegon the Conqueror had&nbsp;
a prophetic dream of the White Walker invasion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.520
This awful vision inspired him to invade&nbsp;
Westeros as a way to save mankind from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.640
destruction. Standing beside the skull of&nbsp;
Aegon's dragon, Balerion, Viserys says:

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.160
"Aegon saw absolute darkness&nbsp;
riding on those winds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.280
and whatever dwells within will&nbsp;
destroy the world of the living."

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.440
Viserys goes on to say that Aegon called his&nbsp;
dream "the Song of Ice and Fire," and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.800
the only way for mankind to survive this wintry&nbsp;
threat is with a Targaryen on the Iron Throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.520
This revelation changes everything we thought&nbsp;
we knew about the history of House Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.120
as well as their relationship&nbsp;
to the mysterious White Walkers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.600
House of the Dragon essentially reveals&nbsp;
that the Targaryen dynasty was established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:55.440
to protect men from extinction, not out of Aegon&nbsp;
the Conqueror's desire for control and plunder.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.400
This reveal also establishes that the fates of&nbsp;
the White Walkers and the Targaryens have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.920
intertwined for centuries, providing more concrete&nbsp;
understanding of why the Targaryen lineage is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.760
wrapped up in the legend of Azor Ahai, a legendary&nbsp;
hero prophesied to save the world. Furthermore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.000
"The Heirs of the Dragon" makes it clear that&nbsp;
this secret has been passed down through each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.600
Targaryen generation, from one ruler to the next.&nbsp;
Considering the fact that this knowledge appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.160
to have been lost by the time the events of Game&nbsp;
of Thrones come around, it will be interesting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.640
see what becomes of this particular plot&nbsp;
point as House of the Dragon continues.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.640
No matter what happens, it's remarkable that&nbsp;
House of the Dragon has already managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:43.920
clear up one of the many mysteries&nbsp;
left unresolved by Game of Thrones.

